  "question": {
    "text": "<strong>Paragraph:</strong>\nA carbonyl compound $P$, which gives positive iodoform test, undergoes reaction with MeMgBr followed by dehydration to give an olefin $Q$. Ozonolysis of $Q$ leads to a dicarbonyl compound $R$, which undergoes intramolecular aldol reaction to give predominantly $S$.\n\n$$\nP \\underset{\\text { (ii) } \\mathrm{H}^{+}, \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}}{\\stackrel{\\text { (i) } \\mathrm{MeMgBr}}{\\longrightarrow}} \\mathrm{Q} \\underset{\\text { Heat }}{\\stackrel{\\mathrm{O}_3 / \\mathrm{Zn}-\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}}{\\longrightarrow}} \\mathrm{P}\n$$\n(iii) $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{SO}_4$ /Heat<strong>Question:</strong>\n$$\n\\text { The structures of the products } Q \\text { and } R \\text {, respectively, are }\n$$",
